<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Disabled is asserted; Trip Output OFF; Valve Status shown but Alarms disabled]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OFF-SCAN (EnableIn is False) STATUS
============================================================
"Lurking" Program Commands are cleared if they are set as "Edge" triggered
(cleared by this object as received).
(Lurking Acknowledge Commands are left to perform their action.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)OTU(PCmd_Trip);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Operator Commands are cleared, as well as Program Reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(OCmd_Trip) OTU(OCmd_Bypass) OTU(OCmd_Check) OTU(MCmd_Disable) ,OTU(MCmd_Enable) OTU(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Since we're not processing Operator Commands, we're not READY for any of them either!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Rdy_Trip) OTU(Rdy_Bypass) OTU(Rdy_Check) OTU(Rdy_Disable) ,OTU(Rdy_Enable) OTU(Rdy_Reset) OTU(Rdy_ResetAckAll) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SIMULATION INPUTS
============================================================
If the valve is in simulation, its position can be set by triggering one of the
simulation inputs.

If the Inp_SimOpen input is triggered, set the valve to simulate Full Open.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Inp_SimOpen)OTL(Wrk_SimOpen)OTU(Wrk_SimClosed);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Inp_SimClose input is triggered, set the valve to simulate Full Closed.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Inp_SimClose)OTL(Wrk_SimClosed)OTU(Wrk_SimOpen);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
LIMIT SWITCH FEEDBACK DETERMINATION
============================================================
This first "Open" feedback is a copy of the Open Limit Switch, if it is being
used, or a copy of the OPPOSITE of the Closed Limit Switch, if ONLY the
Closed Limit Switch is being used.

If the Valve is being simulated or has no limit switch feedback,
use the Open Sim bit from above.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Cfg_UseOpenLS) XIC(Inp_OpenLS) ,XIO(Cfg_UseOpenLS) XIC(Cfg_UseClosedLS) XIO(Inp_ClosedLS) ] ,[XIC(Inp_Sim) ,XIO(Cfg_UseOpenLS) XIO(Cfg_UseClosedLS) ] XIC(Wrk_SimOpen) ]OTE(Wrk_OpenFdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This first "Closed" feedback is a copy of the Closed Limit Switch, if it is being
used, or a copy of the OPPOSITE of the Open Limit Switch, if ONLY the
Open Limit Switch is being used.

If the Valve is being simulated or has no limit switch feedback,
use the Closed Sim bit from above.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Cfg_UseClosedLS) XIC(Inp_ClosedLS) ,XIO(Cfg_UseClosedLS) XIC(Cfg_UseOpenLS) XIO(Inp_OpenLS) ] ,[XIC(Inp_Sim) ,XIO(Cfg_UseClosedLS) XIO(Cfg_UseOpenLS) ] XIC(Wrk_SimClosed) ]OTE(Wrk_ClosedFdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
VALVE FEEDBACK STATUS
============================================================
This rung generates the Valve Feedback Status bits and Enumeration Value:
Limit Switch Fail, if the Limit Switches are in the fail position (won't be seen in Simulation)
Opened, if the valve is confirmed opened
Closed, if the valve is confirmed closed
Moving, if the Limit Switches show travel]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(Cfg_LSFail) XIC(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIC(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_LSFail) XIO(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIO(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ] OTE(Sts_LSFail) MOV(3,Val_Fdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIO(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) OTE(Sts_Opened) MOV(2,Val_Fdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) XIO(Wrk_OpenFdbk) OTE(Sts_Closed) MOV(1,Val_Fdbk) ,[XIC(Cfg_LSFail) XIO(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIO(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_LSFail) XIC(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIC(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ] OTE(Sts_Moving) CLR(Val_Fdbk) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reset the fault condition and simulation / command retrigger timers.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added clearing of Transit Stall check timer.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[RES(Wrk_TripFailT)RES(Wrk_TransitStallT)RES(Wrk_SimFdbkT);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the device can be tripped, trip it to disable it when Disabled (EnableInFalse).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_HasTrip)OTE(Out_Trip);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Show the motor as Disabled and Not Ready, not Available, and with no
Maintenance Bypass breadcrumb.
Clear remaining Status bits.
Show the enumerated motor command as NONE.
Show the enumerated motor status as DISABLED.
Show the enumerated motor fault status as NONE.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTL(Sts_Disabled) OTL(Sts_NotRdy) OTU(Sts_MaintByp) ,OTL(Nrdy_Disabled) OTU(Nrdy_CfgErr) OTU(Nrdy_Intlk) ,OTU(Nrdy_Trip) OTU(Nrdy_Fail) OTU(Nrdy_IOFault) ,OTU(Sts_Tripping) ,CLR(Val_Cmd) MOV(33,Val_Sts) CLR(Val_Fault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the Alarms and the Notify Status, and show the Alarms Inhibited breadcrumb.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Transit Stall Status and Alarm.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Alm_TripFail) OTU(Alm_TransitStall) OTU(Alm_IntlkTrip) OTU(Alm_IOFault) ,OTU(Sts_TripFail) OTU(Sts_TransitStall) OTU(Sts_IntlkTrip) OTU(Sts_IOFault) ,OTL(Sts_AlmInh) CLR(Val_Notify) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENUMERATED STATUS VALUES
============================================================
Source and Quality (Srcq) for Val_InpPV
Start with the Srcq from the Input Channel object if it's available.
Otherwise, start based on bad/uncertain input bits.

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_SrcQ) ,[XIO(Cfg_HasOpenLS) ,XIO(Cfg_HasClosedLS) ] MOV(1,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Err_Has) MOV(35,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(9,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ_IO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality for primary values / status (SrcQ)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(20,SrcQ);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Normal Scan: monitor hand-operated valve]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
P_ValveHO:  PROCESS -- HAND OPERATED VALVE (monitor)
============================================================
Revision 3.1-02 Release  2014-09-30:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V1.x, V2.x Revision History archived.
V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib. Using P_Alarm V3.0. Added Transit Stall
Status and Alarm.
V3.0-01  2013-07-31:  Modified Parameter descriptions only.
V3.0-02  2013-09-03:  Modified Parameter descriptions only.
V3.0-03  2013-10-30:  Corrected Parameter descriptions and
default configuration values for alarms only.
V3.0-04  2014-01-22:  Corrected LSFail logic, default parameter
values for Limit Switches, Cfg_PCmdClear.
V3.1-00  2014-07-08:  Modified to use P_Alarm V3.1; added Not Ready
reason bits (Nrdy_Xxxxx), input source/quality (SrcQ) enum.
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Exposed stall, fail timers ACC/PRE (read-only). Corrections
to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic. Using P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.1-01.
V3.1-02  2014-09-30:  Unchanged, but using P_Alarm V3.1-02.
============================================================
This Instruction monitors a locally- (hand-) operated valve (two position: opened, closed) and provides:

*  Monitoring of valves with 2 limit switches (confirm open, confirm closed, show travel) or
     1 limit switch (confirm open/assume closed, or confirm closed/assume open)
*  Monitoring of I/O communication status and Alarm on communication failure
* For valve with 2 limit switches, monitoring for a Transit Stall condition,
that is, the valve is not fully open or full closed for an excessive amount of time.
*  Option and output to allow TRIPPING the valve to a failure state.

If the option to allow tripping is enabled, this instruction also provides:

*  Trip by Operator, Program or Interlock at any time (no Mode)
*  Support for valves that fail/trip open or failt/trip closed
*  Detection of failure to reach the trip position within a configured time and Trip Failure Alarm
*  Alarm on Interlock initiated Trip if Interlock caused valve to move to trip position
*  Simulation, providing feedback of a working valve while disabling outputs

Alarms are provided by P_Alarm AOI instances.
============================================================
SHOW LOCAL STRINGS
============================================================
The STRINGs containing the text associated with each instance of this
instruction cannot be Input or Output Parameters, because STRINGs are not
 'atomic' types. (Inputs and Outputs must be SINT, INT, DINT, REAL, or BOOL.)

In order to make it easier to find and configure these STRINGs, this rung
was added.  THE JMP (and the LBL on the following rung)
MUST NOT BE REMOVED!!!

To view the STRINGs, go to the instruction instance (in LD or FBD), RIGHT-click
to bring up the context menu and select "Open Instruction Logic".
This rung will appear with the STRING values for the selected instance.
You may double-click the STRING values here to modify them as well.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(SkipText)CONCAT(Cfg_Desc,Cfg_Label,Cfg_Tag)LOWER(Inf_Lib,Inf_Type);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CONFIGURATION
============================================================
If the Valve does not have a Close Limit Switch input,
it cannot be used for Valve feedback checking.

Note that the valve MUST have at least one limit switch.  If this switch
doesn't exist, the other one MUST and MUST be used!

#####  V3.0-00, 2013-06-30:  Checking both cases.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipText)[XIO(Cfg_HasClosedLS) XIC(Cfg_HasOpenLS) OTU(Cfg_UseClosedLS) OTL(Cfg_UseOpenLS) ,XIO(Cfg_HasOpenLS) XIC(Cfg_HasClosedLS) OTU(Cfg_UseOpenLS) OTL(Cfg_UseClosedLS) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These rungs get Configuration data (such as timer presets) and distribute as needed.
Note that some Configuration data are used directly in-place.

Enter the time (in seconds) for the Valve to successfully achieve the trip position before declaring a fault.

If the timer preset calcuated wraps negative (more than 2.14... million seconds), then max out the
Timer Preset.  Note that a negative timer preset will fault the controller!!!

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added lower branch for new Transit Stall Status and Alarm timer config.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[MUL(Cfg_TripFailT,1000,Wrk_TripFailT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_TripFailT.PRE.31) MOV(2147483647,Wrk_TripFailT.PRE) ,MUL(Cfg_TransitStallT,1000,Wrk_TransitStallT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_TransitStallT.PRE.31) MOV(2147483647,Wrk_TransitStallT.PRE) ]OTE(Err_Timer);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Enter the time (in seconds) to echo back the "tripping" state when Tripped in simulation

If the timer preset is invalid, use zero (immediately go to configured trip position).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MUL(Cfg_SimFdbkT,1000,Wrk_SimFdbkT.PRE)XIC(Wrk_SimFdbkT.PRE.31)CLR(Wrk_SimFdbkT.PRE)OTE(Err_Sim);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung generates a summary Bad Config status, simply an OR of the individual bits provided above
(in the Configuration handling section).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasOpenLS) XIO(Cfg_HasClosedLS) OTE(Err_Has) ,XIO(Err_Has) XIO(Cfg_UseOpenLS) XIO(Cfg_UseClosedLS) OTE(Err_Use) ,XIC(Err_Timer) ,XIC(Err_Sim) ,[XIC(TripFail.Sts_Err) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Sts_Err) ,XIC(IOFault.Sts_Err) ] OTE(Err_Alarm) ]OTE(Sts_Err);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SIMULATION INPUTS
============================================================
If the valve is in simulation, its position can be set by triggering one of the
simulation inputs.

If the Inp_SimOpen input is triggered, set the valve to simulate Full Open.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Inp_SimOpen)OTL(Wrk_SimOpen)OTU(Wrk_SimClosed);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Inp_SimClose input is triggered, set the valve to simulate Full Closed.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Inp_SimClose)OTL(Wrk_SimClosed)OTU(Wrk_SimOpen);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SIMULATION TIMER
============================================================
If in Simulation and a Valve Trip is in progress, run a Trip Feedback Simulation timer.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Inp_Sim)XIC(Nrdy_Trip)[TON(Wrk_SimFdbkT,?,?) ,XIC(Wrk_SimFdbkT.TT) OTU(Wrk_SimOpen) OTU(Wrk_SimClosed) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When the Simulation Feedback timer goes done, if the valve trips Open, simulate
the valve reaching open, and if the valve trips Closed, simulate reaching closed.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_SimFdbkT.dn)[XIC(Cfg_TripOpen) OTL(Wrk_SimOpen) OTU(Wrk_SimClosed) ,XIO(Cfg_TripOpen) OTL(Wrk_SimClosed) OTU(Wrk_SimOpen) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
LIMIT SWITCH FEEDBACK DETERMINATION
============================================================
If the Valve is being simulated or has no limit switch feedback, use the Sim Timers to provide
"fake" feedback signals based on the simulation time to Open and time to Close.

If the Valve is NOT being simulated and it HAS and IS USING limit switch feedback,
use the state of the limit switch feedback inputs as the Valve position.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Cfg_UseOpenLS) XIC(Inp_OpenLS) ,XIO(Cfg_UseOpenLS) XIO(Inp_ClosedLS) ] ,XIC(Inp_Sim) XIC(Wrk_SimOpen) XIO(Wrk_SimClosed) ]OTE(Wrk_OpenFdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Valve is being simulated or has no limit switch feedback, use the Sim Timers to provide
"fake" feedback signals based on the simulation time to Open and time to Close.

If the Valve is NOT being simulated and it HAS and IS USING limit switch feedback,
use the state of the limit switch feedback inputs as the Valve position.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Cfg_UseClosedLS) XIC(Inp_ClosedLS) ,XIO(Cfg_UseClosedLS) XIO(Inp_OpenLS) ] ,XIC(Inp_Sim) XIC(Wrk_SimClosed) XIO(Wrk_SimOpen) ]OTE(Wrk_ClosedFdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The valve can be configured to have Limit Switch Failure shown for both
limit switches ON or for both switches OFF.

#####  V3.0-04  2014-01-20:  Mod. to not show LS Fail if LS config is bad.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)XIO(Err_Use)XIO(Err_Has)[XIC(Cfg_LSFail) XIC(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIC(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_LSFail) XIO(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIO(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ]OTE(Wrk_LSFailFdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The OTHER (non-failure) state with both switches ON or both switches OFF is
valve IN TRANSIT.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Cfg_LSFail) XIO(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIO(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_LSFail) XIC(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIC(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ] ,XIC(Inp_Sim) XIO(Wrk_SimOpen) XIO(Wrk_SimClosed) ]OTE(Wrk_TravelFdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
VALVE FEEDBACK STATUS
============================================================
This rung generates the Valve Feedback Status bits and Enumeration Value:
Limit Switch Fail, if the Limit Switches are in the fail position (won't be seen in Simulation)
Opened, if the valve is confirmed opened
Closed, if the valve is confirmed closed
Moving, if the Limit Switches show travel]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(Cfg_LSFail) XIC(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIC(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_LSFail) XIO(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIO(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ] MOV(3,Val_Fdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIO(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) MOV(2,Val_Fdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) XIO(Wrk_OpenFdbk) MOV(1,Val_Fdbk) ,[XIC(Cfg_LSFail) XIO(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIO(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_LSFail) XIC(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIC(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ] CLR(Val_Fdbk) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
INTERLOCK / PERMISSIVE BYPASS / CHECK COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Bypass Command bypasses the Bypassable Permissives and Interlocks.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(OCmd_Bypass)OTU(OCmd_Bypass)OTL(Wrk_Bypass);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Check Command enables checking of ALL
Permissives and Interlocks (cancels the bypass).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(OCmd_Check)OTU(OCmd_Check)OTU(Wrk_Bypass);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the internal Bypass flag is set, Bypassable Interlocks and Permissives ARE BYPASSED.
Bypassing is ACTIVE if Bypass selected.  (This object has no Maintenance or Override Mode.)

This is the only Maintenance Bypass function, so show the Maintenance Bypass breadcrumb]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Bypass)OTE(Sts_Bypass)OTE(Sts_BypActive);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Maintenance Bypass function is active, display the Maintenance Bypass
Indicator (triangle symbol) on the graphic symbol.  Bypass functions are:
*  Interlock / Permissive Bypass function is enabled
*  Valve HAS opened position feedback designated by engineer, but
maintenance has selected to NOT USE opened position feedback
*  Valve HAS closed position feedback designated by engineer, but
maintenance has selected to NOT USE closed position feedback]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_Bypass) ,XIC(Cfg_HasOpenLS) XIO(Cfg_UseOpenLS) ,XIC(Cfg_HasClosedLS) XIO(Cfg_UseClosedLS) ]OTE(Sts_MaintByp);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If Trip is used, then the valve trip interlocks can be bypassed or not.
Ready for Interlock / Permissive Bypass if not bypassed.
Ready to cancel Bypass (resume checking) if bypassed.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_HasTrip)[XIO(Wrk_Bypass) OTE(Rdy_Bypass) ,XIC(Wrk_Bypass) OTE(Rdy_Check) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
DEVICE DISABLE/ENABLE COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Disable Command disables the valve so it is always tripped.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCmd_Disable)OTU(MCmd_Disable)OTL(Wrk_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Enable Command cancels the Disable and allows the valve to be manipulated.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(MCmd_Enable) OTU(MCmd_Enable) ,XIO(Cfg_HasTrip) ]OTU(Wrk_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the internal Disabled flag is set, the valve is DISABLED.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Disabled)OTE(Sts_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If Trip is used, then the valve can be enabled or disabled:
Ready to Disable device if in Maintenance Mode and device is NOT Disabled.
Ready to Enable device if in Maintenance Mode and device IS Disabled.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_HasTrip)[XIO(Wrk_Disabled) OTE(Rdy_Disable) ,XIC(Wrk_Disabled) OTE(Rdy_Enable) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM RESET COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
This rung handles the Alarm Reset Input and Commands
and the "Reset and Ack All" Operator Command.

This rung processes received Reset Commands from:

1.  The Operator via HMI Operator Command, or
2.  Higher-level strategies via Program Command
3.  Pushbuttons or other block via Input
4.  Resets initiated by other device Operator Commands (if configured to do so)

and forwards the Reset to ALL Alarms and latched Shed conditions.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added reset of Transit Stall Alarm and its timer.  #####
#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_Reset) ,XIC(OCmd_Trip) XIC(Cfg_OCmdResets) ,XIC(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) [OTL(TripFail.PCmd_Ack) ,OTL(TransitStall.PCmd_Ack) ,OTL(IntlkTrip.PCmd_Ack) ,OTL(IOFault.PCmd_Ack) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Reset) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ,NOP() ] ,XIC(Inp_Reset) ][OTL(TripFail.PCmd_Reset) OTL(TransitStall.PCmd_Reset) OTL(IntlkTrip.PCmd_Reset) OTL(IOFault.PCmd_Reset) ,XIC(Sts_TripFail) RES(Wrk_TripFailT) ,OTU(Nrdy_Fail) OTU(Nrdy_Trip) ,[XIO(Inp_IOFault) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ] OTU(Nrdy_IOFault) ,RES(Wrk_SimFdbkT) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
VALVE COMMANDED TRIP HANDLING
============================================================
If Interlocks are not OK (Non-Bypassable not OK, or bypassable not OK
and not bypassed by Maintenance, Override or Bypass Command), 
OR if the Valve is DISABLED or FAULTED, set it to its FAIL STATE.

If it is NOT in its fail state (if it is energized) and the Interlock
de-energized it, raise the Interlock Trip alarm.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Trip) OTU(OCmd_Trip) ,XIC(PCmd_Trip) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Trip) ,NOP() ] ]XIC(Cfg_HasTrip)OTL(Nrdy_Trip);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Valve was told to Trip and it reached the configured Trip Position,
then Trip is completed (successfully).  Turn off the "Trip in Progress" latch.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasTrip) ,XIC(Cfg_TripOpen) XIC(Wrk_OpenFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_TripOpen) XIC(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ]OTU(Nrdy_Trip);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
VALVE TRIP FAIL DETECTION
============================================================
If the Valve was told to trip and it hasn't reached the trip position, the Wrk_Trip
bit will be set.  Run a Trip Fail timer, and if it goes done, raise the Fail to Trip Status.
Since we're done with this trip (even though it failed), turn off the "Trip in Progress" latch.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Nrdy_Trip)[XIC(Cfg_TripOpen) XIO(Wrk_OpenFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_TripOpen) XIO(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ][TON(Wrk_TripFailT,?,?) ,XIC(Wrk_TripFailT.DN) OTU(Nrdy_Trip) OTE(Sts_TripFail) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
VALVE TRANSIT STALL DETECTION
============================================================
If the Valve was told to trip and it hasn't reached the trip position, the Wrk_Trip
bit will be set.  Run a Trip Fail timer, and if it goes done, raise the Fail to Trip Status.
Since we're done with this trip (even though it failed), turn off the "Trip in Progress" latch.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Transit Stall Status and Alarm.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_TravelFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_LSFailFdbk) ][TON(Wrk_TransitStallT,?,?) ,XIC(Wrk_TransitStallT.DN) OTE(Sts_TransitStall) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SHED ON FAULT LOGIC
============================================================
This rung handles latching in of conditions which are configured to cause
valve to shed (trip).

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_TripFail)XIC(Cfg_ShedOnFailToTrip)OTL(Nrdy_Fail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Valve is NOT READY if:
* Interlocks are not OK and not bypassed
* Non-bypassable Interlocks are not OK
* There's an I/O failure and the valve is NOT being simulated
* The valve has a Shed Fault (fail to trip, I/O fault) that has not been reset
* The valve is disabled.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_Disabled) OTE(Nrdy_Disabled) ,XIC(Sts_Err) OTE(Nrdy_CfgErr) ,[XIO(Inp_IntlkOK) XIO(Wrk_Bypass) ,XIO(Inp_NBIntlkOK) ] [XIC(Cfg_HasTrip) [XIC(Cfg_TripOpen) XIO(Wrk_OpenFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_TripOpen) XIO(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ] OTE(Sts_IntlkTrip) ,OTE(Nrdy_Intlk) ] ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) XIO(Inp_Sim) OTE(Sts_IOFault) XIC(Cfg_ShedOnIOFault) OTL(Nrdy_IOFault) ]OTE(Wrk_NotRdy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Valve is NOT READY if:
* Interlocks are not OK and not bypassed
* Non-bypassable Interlocks are not OK
* There's an I/O failure and the valve is NOT being simulated
* The valve has a Shed Fault (fail to trip, I/O fault) that has not been reset
* The valve is disabled.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_NotRdy) ,XIC(Nrdy_Fail) ,XIC(Nrdy_Trip) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) ]OTE(Sts_NotRdy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
DEVICE COMMAND ENUMERATED VALUE
============================================================
Val_Cmd is the command currently being processed:
0 = None
7 = Trip

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Nrdy_Trip) CLR(Val_Cmd) ,XIC(Nrdy_Trip) MOV(7,Val_Cmd) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OUTPUT GENERATION
============================================================

If the Valve is NOT SIMULATED and HAS THE TRIP FUNCTION WIRED, generate the
appropriate output for the Valve.
If the Valve should be tripped, is disabled or faulted, energize the TRIP output.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_HasTrip)XIO(Inp_Sim)XIC(Sts_NotRdy)OTE(Out_Trip);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
STATUS GENERATION
============================================================

The following rungs generate Status bits for this object.

This rung generates the Valve Monitoring and Trip Status bits:
Open, if the valve is confirmed open and the valve is not tripping
Closed, if the valve is confirmed closed and the valve is not tripping
Limit Switch Fail, if the Limit Switches are in the fail position (won't be seen in Simulation)
Moving, if the Limit Switches show travel and the valve is not tripping
Tripping, if the valve is tripping

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIO(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) XIO(Nrdy_Trip) OTE(Sts_Opened) ,XIC(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) XIO(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIO(Nrdy_Trip) OTE(Sts_Closed) ,XIC(Wrk_LSFailFdbk) OTE(Sts_LSFail) ,XIC(Wrk_TravelFdbk) XIO(Nrdy_Trip) OTE(Sts_Moving) ,XIC(Nrdy_Trip) OTE(Sts_Tripping) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Val_Sts is the current device status, as determined by this AOI,
based on its knowledge of commands executed and feedback.
(This is the status that should be monitored by, for example, FT Historian.)
0 = Powerup / Unknown
1 = Closed
2 = Opened
8 = Moving
13 = Tripping
33 = Device Disabled

Val_Fault is the current device fault status, as determined by this AOI,
based on its knowledge of commands executed and feedback.
(This is the fault status that should be monitored by, for example, FT Historian.)
0 = None
16 = Transit Stall
18 = Fail to Trip
32 = I/O Fault (from Input)
34 = Configuration Error

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Transit Stall enumeration value.  #####
#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Sts) CLR(Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Sts_Closed) MOV(1,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_Opened) MOV(2,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_Moving) MOV(8,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_Tripping) MOV(13,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_TransitStall) MOV(16,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Sts_TripFail) MOV(18,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Nrdy_IOFault) MOV(32,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Sts_Disabled) MOV(33,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_Err) MOV(34,Wrk_Fault) ,MOV(Wrk_Sts,Val_Sts) MOV(Wrk_Fault,Val_Fault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENUMERATED SOURCE / QUALITY VALUES
============================================================
Source and Quality for Input / Output values / status (SrcQ_IO)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_SrcQ) ,[XIO(Cfg_HasOpenLS) ,XIO(Cfg_HasClosedLS) ] MOV(1,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Err_Has) MOV(35,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(9,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ_IO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality for primary values / status (SrcQ)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[MOV(SrcQ_IO,Wrk_SrcQ) ,[XIC(Cfg_HasOpenLS) XIO(Cfg_UseOpenLS) ,XIC(Cfg_HasClosedLS) XIO(Cfg_UseClosedLS) ] MOV(18,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OPERATOR COMMAND READIES
============================================================

Ready to Open if in Operator Manual, Closed, and Permissives and Interlocks are OK.

Ready to Close if in Operator Manual and (Opened or Opening).

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_HasTrip)[XIO(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIC(Cfg_TripOpen) ,XIO(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) XIO(Cfg_TripOpen) ]XIO(Wrk_NotRdy)[XIO(Sts_NotRdy) ,XIC(Cfg_OCmdResets) ]OTE(Rdy_Trip);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="38" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM PROCESSING
============================================================
Pass the Cfg_PCmdClear configuration down to each P_Alarm instance.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(TripFail.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(TransitStall.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(IntlkTrip.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(IOFault.Cfg_PCmdClear);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="39" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the valve does not have two independent limit switches, the "moving" position cannot
(will not) be detected, so a Transit Stall is meaningless and its Alarm should not exist.

#####  V3.0-00, 2013-06-30:  Added rung for new Transit Stall Status and Alarm  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasOpenLS) ,XIO(Cfg_HasClosedLS) ]OTU(Cfg_HasTransitStallAlm);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="40" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The various alarms are ALWAYS allowed to Exist (Cfg_HasXxxAlarm can be 1), EXCEPT:
* If the valve DOES NOT HAVE TRIP CAPABILITY, the Fail to Trip and Interlock Trip
alarms will never occur and should not exist.  (If the trip function exists, 
these alarms must be allowed to exist.)
* If the valve DOES NOT HAVE BOTH LIMIT SWITCHES, the "moving" state cannot
be detected and the Transit Stall alarm will never occur and should not
exist.  (If both limit switches exist, this alarm must be allowed to exist.)

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added PCfg_AllowExist on P_Alarm 3.0.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTL(IOFault.PCfg_AllowExist) ,XIC(Cfg_HasTrip) OTE(IntlkTrip.PCfg_AllowExist) OTE(TripFail.PCfg_AllowExist) ,XIC(Cfg_HasClosedLS) XIC(Cfg_HasOpenLS) OTE(TransitStall.PCfg_AllowExist) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="41" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Motor Failed to Trip Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(TripFail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="42" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Transit Stall Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Transit Stall Alarm.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(TransitStall);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="43" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Interlock Trip Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(IntlkTrip);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="44" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle I/O Fault Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(IOFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="45" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If ANY alarm is Disabled, Inhibited or Suppressed, set the Alarm Inhibit
summary status bit (which puts the "I" box on the graphic symbol).

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Transit Stall Alarm.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(TripFail.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(TransitStall.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(IOFault.Sts_AlmInh) ]OTE(Sts_AlmInh);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="46" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
NOTIFICATION VALUE
============================================================
Indicate the current alarm notification level as the max of any of the alarms,
and set the low-order bit for reset or ack required:
0 = Not in alarm, acknowledged
1 = Not in alarm, unacknowledged or reset required
2 = Low severity alarm, acknowledged
3 = Low severity alarm, unacknowledged
4 = Medium severity alarm, acknowledged
5 = Medium severity alarm, unacknowledged
6 = High severity alarm, acknowledged
7 = High severity alarm, unacknowledged
8 = Urgent severity alarm, acknowledged
9 = Urgent severity alarm, unacknowledged

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Separated Reset Reqd functions from Val_Notify  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(TripFail.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(TripFail.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(TransitStall.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(TransitStall.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(IntlkTrip.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(IntlkTrip.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(IOFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(IOFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,[XIC(TripFail.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(TransitStall.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(IOFault.Val_Notify.0) ] OTE(Wrk_Notify.0) ,MOV(Wrk_Notify,Val_Notify) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="47" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung identifies:
* if any alarm reset or other reset is required; and
* if any reset or acknowledge from the operator is required.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added Sts_ShedResetReqd, split from Val_Notify logic (above).  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(TripFail.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(TransitStall.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(IOFault.Rdy_Ack) ] ,[XIC(TripFail.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(TransitStall.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(IOFault.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(Nrdy_Fail) ,XIC(Nrdy_IOFault) XIO(Sts_IOFault) ] OTE(Rdy_Reset) ]OTE(Rdy_ResetAckAll);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Prescan" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Clear "lurking" Commands]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
PRESCAN (POWERUP) HANDLING
============================================================
"Lurking" Program Commands are cleared if they are set as "Edge" triggered
(cleared by this object as received).
(Lurking Acknowledge Commands are left to perform their action.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)OTU(PCmd_Trip);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Operator Commands are cleared, as well as Program Reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(OCmd_Trip) OTU(OCmd_Bypass) OTU(OCmd_Check) OTU(MCmd_Disable) ,OTU(MCmd_Enable) OTU(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the latched Trip command and latched Shed faults.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Nrdy_Trip)OTU(Nrdy_Fail)OTU(Nrdy_IOFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[All Outputs are de-energized on Prescan.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Out_Trip);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[On Prescan, clear the following:
Val_Cmd (no command active)
Val_Fdbk (device position not determined)
Val_Sts (device status powerup / unknown)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Val_Cmd)CLR(Val_Fdbk)CLR(Val_Sts);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_40"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_20"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_12"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_16"/>
<Dependency Type="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="P_Alarm"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
